// Shadow Credentials Added via msDS-KeyCredentialLink
// Detects a write to the msDS-KeyCredentialLink attribute of a user or computer object. Adding a key credential registers an attacker-controlled certificate for Kerberos PKINIT, giving them a way to authenticate as that principal and recover its NTLM hash without ever changing a password. Almost nothing writes this attribute outside Windows Hello for Business enrollment.
// techniques: T1556,T1098   severity: critical   status: experimental
// validate: Atomic Red Team T1556
//   Whisker.exe add /target:DC01$
//   pywhisker.py -d domain -u user -p pass --target victim --action add
// source: rules/credential-access/shadow-credentials-key-credential-link.yml  (GENERATED, do not edit by hand)
SecurityEvent
| where ((EventID =~ "5136") and (AttributeLDAPDisplayName =~ "msDS-KeyCredentialLink"))
